      "writtenOn": "2022-02-28T15:33:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why did you change the variable name from `errcode` to `match_result`? If I read it correctly, `EC_MKBP_FP_ERRCODE` is returning an error code. \n\nMore specifically, I believe we expect this to be a `match_errcode` as the error codes are defined in such a way that the value returned by `EC_MKBP_FP_ERRCODE` depends upon state of bits 27-31 (i.e. a value of 1 could mean `EC_MKBP_FP_ENROLL_LOW_QUALITY` if enrollment is active or `EC_MKBP_FP_ERR_MATCH_NO_INTERNAL` if matching is set). Is this right @tomhughes? Is there a reason we\u0027re reusing some of the error codes rather than just enumerating all errors? It appears that we presently only have 14 error codes (out of a possible 15) and some spare bits if we needed future growth.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 846,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 846,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "962192ad46567b219dae02dc5b13c93270584c24",
